WEBVTT

01:30.240 --> 01:36.490
#3 The King's Homecoming.

01:40.830 --> 01:42.990
It's good that we were 
able to deliver in time.

01:42.990 --> 01:43.710
Yeah.

01:44.030 --> 01:48.500
I was shocked when I saw you come running. 
I didn't know you could do that.

01:48.910 --> 01:51.500
You just focus wind mana on your feet.

01:51.910 --> 01:55.760
It's an application of something Ar... 
something you taught me a while ago.

01:57.250 --> 01:59.260
I didn't realize that was an option.

02:03.510 --> 02:05.020
Hey there, Jasmine.

02:07.900 --> 02:08.820
Do you know him?

02:09.240 --> 02:12.520
That's Brald. An AA-rank adventurer.

02:12.900 --> 02:14.830
It's an honor that you're 
familiar with me.

02:15.370 --> 02:17.530
I'm actually here today to ask a favor.

02:18.190 --> 02:20.020
I've got a lead on an incredible treasure.

02:20.330 --> 02:22.030
I'm hoping you'll help me collect.

02:24.940 --> 02:27.540
<i>Another AA-ranker, like Jasmine.</i>

02:28.510 --> 02:30.530
<i>He's almost certainly of great skill.</i>

02:30.970 --> 02:36.410
<i>But for some reason, the sight of him 
near her makes my heart grow tense.</i>

02:53.130 --> 02:55.570
Are you ready, Arthur?

02:55.790 --> 02:57.320
Whenever you are, Adam.

02:57.620 --> 02:58.840
Let's go, then!

03:18.750 --> 03:19.640
<i>I have him.</i>

03:37.070 --> 03:37.780
<i>He's coming.</i>

03:38.850 --> 03:40.650
<i>Will he thrust or sweep?</i>

03:42.920 --> 03:43.910
<i>Neither.</i>

03:54.950 --> 03:56.340
You actually blocked it.

03:56.780 --> 03:58.340
Just barely.

03:58.650 --> 04:01.350
I'm impressed you knew I was 
going to strike from up high.

04:01.350 --> 04:03.340
Just a lucky guess.

04:03.700 --> 04:06.160
It's been a long time since 
anyone blocked that move.

04:06.160 --> 04:07.850
You've gotten stronger again.

04:08.120 --> 04:09.140
Thanks.

04:09.850 --> 04:11.520
That was overkill.

04:11.520 --> 04:13.490
Do you understand the 
concept of holding back?

04:13.490 --> 04:14.940
Hey, you saw the kid!

04:14.940 --> 04:17.300
He's no "little monster" anymore.

04:17.300 --> 04:18.610
Just a plain monster!

04:18.610 --> 04:20.860
Quit picking on my brother!

04:21.190 --> 04:22.600
Are you hurt?

04:22.600 --> 04:24.360
My hands are tingling 
a bit, but that's all.

04:24.360 --> 04:27.070
I notice you don't tend to 
get angry at Adam, Alice.

04:27.070 --> 04:28.900
He was serious just now.

04:28.900 --> 04:31.620
It was for the sake of 
training. He had to be.

04:31.620 --> 04:35.020
Besides, what really bothers me is the 
idea of him doing something dangerous

04:35.020 --> 04:37.250
where I can't look out for him.

04:39.250 --> 04:42.390
Arthur, archery training is next.

04:42.390 --> 04:44.510
And then earth magic.

04:44.810 --> 04:47.510
And lastly, I'll show you
 some wind magic.

04:48.220 --> 04:49.420
Please, do!

04:50.410 --> 04:52.060
<i>The Twinhorns.</i>

04:52.850 --> 04:58.520
<i>The training they could offer me as 
AA-rank adventurers was of great value.</i>

05:03.660 --> 05:06.780
I'm sorry. You probably want to 
join in on Arthur's training.

05:07.180 --> 05:10.780
No, it's fine. But what did 
you want to talk about?

05:11.240 --> 05:12.860
Are you familiar with Brald?

05:13.390 --> 05:14.170
Yeah.

05:17.040 --> 05:19.340
He's made a career of 
fighting on the front lines,

05:19.340 --> 05:23.470
often in the most dangerous position.

05:24.050 --> 05:29.050
But in spite of that, he manages to clear 
most of his quests without a scratch.

05:31.710 --> 05:35.530
Brald Ironsides, the Great Wall,
 the White Knight...

05:35.530 --> 05:38.290
He's earned a lot of renown, 
to say nothing of trust

05:38.290 --> 05:43.050
from both the guild and other adventurers.

05:44.670 --> 05:45.820
What's he like?

05:45.820 --> 05:49.270
Just like the rumors say. 
He's a pleasant fellow.

05:49.270 --> 05:54.030
And very skilled. Even I'd have 
trouble getting past his shield.

05:54.710 --> 05:56.080
What about him, though?

05:56.660 --> 05:58.370
He's invited me on a quest.

05:59.260 --> 06:03.580
That's odd. He has a party of his own.

06:04.950 --> 06:08.490
It's not just me, either. 
He's been asking around.

06:08.830 --> 06:10.450
So, it got me curious.

06:11.650 --> 06:14.360
A reason for suddenly recruiting talent...

06:15.070 --> 06:16.580
What's your take, Jasmine?

06:16.580 --> 06:18.350
Replacements for injured party members?

06:18.650 --> 06:23.540
No. His party knows what they're doing.
That'd be hard to imagine.

06:24.060 --> 06:24.860
Anything else?

06:25.230 --> 06:28.110
Other than that... a disagreement.

06:28.110 --> 06:31.490
That's the most typical reason 
that parties break up, after all.

06:31.490 --> 06:35.280
And it's likely this quest he's 
talking about was the cause.

06:35.280 --> 06:37.430
That's a fair deduction to make,

06:37.430 --> 06:39.650
but we shouldn't jump to conclusions.

06:40.370 --> 06:42.790
That sort of thing can you 
give you tunnel vision.

06:43.110 --> 06:45.890
A good leader must keep a cool head 
and approach things even-handedly.

06:46.410 --> 06:50.120
That's something I tried to keep in mind
 when I became the group's leader.

06:50.120 --> 06:52.890
Not that it was easy, mind you.

06:52.890 --> 06:55.140
Yeah. You paid almost all 
your attention to Alice.

06:55.140 --> 06:57.780
Could you not bring that up?

06:58.860 --> 07:02.510
I'm going to do a bit more digging. 
Seeing as I'm the leader now.

07:02.510 --> 07:04.770
Right. Look after Arthur for me.

07:07.280 --> 07:09.880
Okay, I should get going, too.

07:23.050 --> 07:25.450
Who was it that asked 
me about holding back?

07:25.450 --> 07:27.050
Sorry, I got carried away.

07:27.050 --> 07:30.920
I didn't think Arthur had 
gotten that strong.

07:31.200 --> 07:32.700
We really are sorry.

07:32.700 --> 07:34.800
No picking on my big brother!

07:35.090 --> 07:37.000
You guys...

07:37.000 --> 07:40.810
Arthur! You all done 
warming up? Looks like it.

07:41.100 --> 07:43.270
Now it's my turn!

07:44.060 --> 07:46.010
Training is over for today!

07:46.010 --> 07:47.070
It's over!

07:47.950 --> 07:49.280
But I didn't get to...

07:49.280 --> 07:50.940
I said, it's over, and I meant it.

07:50.940 --> 07:51.820
Over!

07:52.080 --> 07:54.500
But... our father/son time...

07:54.500 --> 07:56.840
It'll have to be something 
other than training.

07:56.840 --> 07:57.830
Something else!

07:58.950 --> 07:59.870
Fine...

08:00.780 --> 08:03.700
You okay? You can keep 
resting if you need to.

08:03.700 --> 08:05.700
That might sound odd,
coming from me.

08:05.700 --> 08:07.550
No, it's all right.

08:07.870 --> 08:08.840
Where's Jasmine?

08:09.230 --> 08:11.340
She had something to look into.

08:11.340 --> 08:15.560
Okay, Arthur, you're going 
to keep us company.

08:15.560 --> 08:16.850
You sure are!

08:16.850 --> 08:18.740
Okay.

08:18.740 --> 08:20.920
<i>Sometimes I'm struck by how odd it feels.</i>

08:21.350 --> 08:25.970
<i>These words that come so 
naturally, and are so simple.</i>

08:26.790 --> 08:32.360
<i>How long will it be, I wonder, before 
these kinds of things seem to fit me?</i>

08:36.840 --> 08:37.740
<i>Mom.</i>

08:45.690 --> 08:48.130
Here's a quest for 
gathering medicinal herbs.

08:48.430 --> 08:49.610
Asinine.

08:49.610 --> 08:52.380
How about searching for a lost mana beast?

08:52.380 --> 08:53.380
Pathetic.

08:53.380 --> 08:56.590
There's also a mage who is 
requesting help with moving!

08:56.590 --> 08:57.640
Out of the question!

08:57.950 --> 09:00.700
Then, sir, what about cleaning the sewers?

09:00.700 --> 09:02.390
Are you mocking me?!

09:03.420 --> 09:05.610
Are there no decent quests?

09:05.610 --> 09:08.150
Terribly sorry, Master Lucas.

09:08.150 --> 09:12.410
With all the trouble lately, 
several adventurers have died,

09:12.410 --> 09:15.680
so the guild is taking more 
time to look into requests.

09:15.680 --> 09:19.410
The issue with mana beasts more 
dangerous than anticipated showing up?

09:19.910 --> 09:22.410
I'd make short work of them, regardless.

09:22.410 --> 09:24.790
Well said, Master Lucas!

09:25.850 --> 09:27.500
I was hoping to tackle a major quest

09:27.500 --> 09:30.670
before enrolling in the 
academy, but at this rate...

09:32.710 --> 09:36.430
I have something that might 
be worth your time, then.

09:36.700 --> 09:38.280
What is it, Shiun?

09:38.280 --> 09:41.430
Are you familiar with 
an adventurer named Brald?

09:41.430 --> 09:43.180
Isn't he AA-ranked?

09:43.420 --> 09:47.940
Yes. He's apparently been  
recruiting party members

09:48.230 --> 09:52.620
as part of a raid on an undiscovered, 
high-ranked dungeon.

09:53.020 --> 09:54.440
In secret from the guild.

09:55.790 --> 09:59.850
Someone with your power should 
have no trouble getting recruited.

10:00.430 --> 10:02.200
Sounds interesting!

10:02.200 --> 10:03.810
Young master, you can't!

10:03.810 --> 10:06.960
Quests unauthorized by the 
guild are much too dangerous!

10:07.190 --> 10:08.130
Silence!

10:09.700 --> 10:13.540
Shiun, you're more useful than I thought.

10:13.540 --> 10:15.420
When my father sent you here,

10:15.420 --> 10:17.540
I'd have sworn you were 
nothing more than a babysitter.

10:18.070 --> 10:19.580
Thank you, sir.

10:21.420 --> 10:22.470
I know!

10:23.140 --> 10:24.690
Young master! Where are going?

10:24.690 --> 10:26.730
Wait for us!

10:26.500 --> 10:27.460
Young Master!

10:27.460 --> 10:28.900
Young Master?!

10:28.900 --> 10:30.490
Young Master, please wait for us!

10:51.900 --> 10:53.750
Oh, it looks cute.

10:57.760 --> 10:59.930
But why?

10:59.930 --> 11:03.050
We really need to teach you 
about more than adventuring.

11:03.050 --> 11:05.350
Arthur, what are we here for today?

11:05.350 --> 11:07.140
Uh...

11:09.110 --> 11:11.020
You look pretty, Eleanor.

11:13.520 --> 11:17.730
Isn't that nice, Eleanor? Is that the 
dress you want to wear for your birthday?

11:20.310 --> 11:24.350
<i>The process of aging means 
getting closer to adulthood.</i>

11:24.680 --> 11:27.540
<i>I suppose "pretty" is an 
appropriate word, in that sense.</i>

11:28.140 --> 11:30.720
<i>Fighting a beast would 
be easier than this.</i>

11:30.720 --> 11:33.010
Next, let's pick out some shoes.

11:33.010 --> 11:33.790
There's a next?

11:34.130 --> 11:36.250
Well, obviously we weren't 
just picking out a dress.

11:36.250 --> 11:39.550
Shoes, accessories... we'll need to 
think of something for her hair, too.

11:39.550 --> 11:41.880
Sure, of course.

11:43.300 --> 11:44.870
Come on, Arthur!

11:46.140 --> 11:48.270
<i>There's no escape for me.</i>

11:50.660 --> 11:53.560
So, Tessia, did you finally see Arthur?

11:53.560 --> 11:57.820
It's the funniest thing. I almost did, 
but there was this interruption...

11:58.190 --> 12:01.320
If she had seen him, she wouldn't 
be here having this conversation.

12:01.320 --> 12:06.320
Fey, the first thing I'm going to 
do when I become queen is exile you.

12:06.680 --> 12:09.110
Wow. She declared herself a tyrant.

12:09.110 --> 12:11.580
The revolution will need to 
come sooner than I planned.

12:12.970 --> 12:15.240
Why can't I just see him?

12:15.240 --> 12:16.680
Maybe it wasn't meant to happen.

12:16.680 --> 12:19.090
I miss him so bad, too.

12:19.090 --> 12:20.860
I would just give up.

12:20.860 --> 12:24.840
The princess commands you 
two to be nicer about this.

12:25.100 --> 12:27.530
I'm sure you'll see him!

12:27.530 --> 12:30.350
I bet he misses you just as much!

12:30.350 --> 12:33.850
Right?! You two think so, too, right?!

12:34.110 --> 12:36.700
<i>Should we be worried that our princess</i>

12:36.700 --> 12:40.030
<i>lit up at the sound of 
words she made us say?</i>

12:40.030 --> 12:44.360
<i>Some words can offer salvation, 
even if they're falsehoods.</i>

12:44.750 --> 12:48.370
More importantly, has Elder Virion 
sent any word of another quest?

12:48.370 --> 12:50.830
We have to wait until he's finished 
investigating, apparently.

12:50.830 --> 12:54.860
Well, I wouldn't want to run into 
another weird mana beast, sure.

12:54.860 --> 12:58.880
The guild has been looking into it,
 but with nothing to show so far.

13:00.550 --> 13:03.380
I don't know what the big deal is. 
I can beat anything we come across.

13:03.380 --> 13:06.500
You genuinely seem to forget the 
position you're in at times.

13:06.500 --> 13:09.390
Even coming close to 
disaster is bad enough.

13:13.740 --> 13:15.140
Hey, it's Arthur.

13:15.140 --> 13:16.710
What?! Where?

13:16.710 --> 13:17.670
Over there.

13:21.500 --> 13:22.570
Where'd he go?!

13:24.850 --> 13:29.710
No, he was really there.
Please stop staring daggers at me!

13:37.650 --> 13:39.310
They really are pretty expensive.

13:39.310 --> 13:40.380
Arthur!

13:41.330 --> 13:43.170
Are you looking for a dimensional ring?

13:43.170 --> 13:46.950
Yeah. I had always intended to get one.

13:47.310 --> 13:50.430
I'm curious, how much space 
does the cheapest one have?

13:53.180 --> 13:55.270
For ten gold pieces?

13:55.270 --> 13:57.440
My bow wouldn't fit in one of those.

13:57.870 --> 14:00.060
<i>That'd be of no use at all.</i>

14:01.980 --> 14:02.940
How about that one?

14:03.190 --> 14:06.950
That would store everything you'd 
need for camping overnight.

14:07.290 --> 14:09.590
And the price reflects it.

14:29.560 --> 14:31.970
Yeah. It really is expensive.

14:32.260 --> 14:33.610
Yeah.

14:35.580 --> 14:37.480
There he is!

14:37.480 --> 14:39.870
Mom, I found Arthur!

14:39.870 --> 14:42.730
Oh, and he's with Helen and Angela.

14:42.950 --> 14:46.210
Did you slip out from helping shop?

14:46.210 --> 14:49.610
That's no good! You're supposed 
to help through the whole process.

14:50.290 --> 14:51.770
I know.

14:57.750 --> 14:59.780
I'm exhausted.

15:01.990 --> 15:03.410
Sorry, Sylvie.

15:04.500 --> 15:07.240
<i>Welcome back, Arthur. What's wrong?</i>

15:07.240 --> 15:09.310
<i>This "family time" stuff.</i>

15:09.310 --> 15:11.760
<i>The two of them are a little too 
strong, so I'm exhausted now.</i>

15:11.760 --> 15:16.420
<i>You can't blame them. Alice and 
Eleanor both missed you a lot.</i>

15:16.420 --> 15:19.140
<i>I know, and I missed them too.</i>

15:20.450 --> 15:22.910
<i>Hey, we're going adventuring 
again soon, right?</i>

15:22.910 --> 15:24.650
<i>When do we leave? Right now?</i>

15:25.350 --> 15:29.510
<i>Adventures are on hold for now. 
A lot of stuff needs to be prepared.</i>

15:29.510 --> 15:30.900
<i>Are you that hot to 
head out again?</i>

15:30.900 --> 15:33.400
<i>I just get hungry so fast lately.</i>

15:33.400 --> 15:34.410
<i>It's weird.</i>

15:34.410 --> 15:36.210
<i>Am I not feeding you enough?</i>

15:36.210 --> 15:40.660
<i>It's not about food! I want to eat 
more of those round, sparkly things.</i>

15:41.300 --> 15:45.610
<i>You're craving mana cores? Well, we 
definitely need to start adventuring again.</i>

15:45.610 --> 15:48.860
<i>You could eat us into bankruptcy 
around here, Sylvie.</i>

15:49.740 --> 15:50.800
<i>But...</i>

15:50.800 --> 15:52.430
<i>What's wrong?</i>

15:53.560 --> 15:55.730
<i>It's almost been two years.</i>

15:57.180 --> 16:01.960
<i>I'm only supposed to be an adventurer 
until I enroll at Xyrus Academy.</i>

16:02.410 --> 16:04.690
<i>The time limit for 
that is approaching.</i>

16:06.470 --> 16:09.690
<i>This next quest will 
probably be my last one.</i>

16:10.460 --> 16:12.200
<i>And when that's over...</i>

16:13.030 --> 16:16.200
I wonder what Jasmine thinks about it.

16:17.540 --> 16:18.820
Jasmine, are you there?

16:19.180 --> 16:20.450
Arthur?!

16:20.450 --> 16:22.110
Come on in!

16:22.110 --> 16:23.810
Yeah, come in!

16:23.810 --> 16:25.000
N-Now hold on...

16:42.070 --> 16:45.880
Since she's always looking out for you,
 we wanted to pay her back.

16:45.880 --> 16:47.730
Mom and I picked it out!

16:48.110 --> 16:49.740
I see.

16:53.900 --> 16:55.990
<i>I had learned.</i>

16:56.350 --> 17:00.120
<i>Eleanor, who is a child, 
disliked being treated as such.</i>

17:00.440 --> 17:02.650
<i>Which would imply that 
Jasmine, who is an adult...</i>

17:03.720 --> 17:05.640
You look really cute, Jasmine.

17:12.520 --> 17:13.500
Huh?

17:13.860 --> 17:16.360
That Jasmine. She was so embarrassed.

17:16.360 --> 17:18.040
She really was.

17:18.040 --> 17:20.510
I needed to talk to her, though.

17:27.030 --> 17:28.900
What are you going to do 
about Brald's invitation?

17:29.640 --> 17:31.910
Honestly? I don't think I should accept.

17:31.910 --> 17:33.090
Why not?

17:33.090 --> 17:34.530
I did some digging.

17:35.170 --> 17:40.230
Brald's doing this on his own. 
His usual party won't be participating.

17:40.610 --> 17:43.010
That's why he turned to you.

17:43.330 --> 17:46.530
Adventurers need to be a bit 
cowardly in order to survive.

17:47.110 --> 17:49.540
Yeah. You're right.

17:50.270 --> 17:52.300
You want to accept, don't you?

17:53.500 --> 17:56.300
I can tell. We've been 
together long enough.

17:59.800 --> 18:05.140
<i>"Avoid danger." That was something 
I learned in my prior life.</i>

18:05.810 --> 18:11.060
<i>But overcoming that danger has 
led to new encounters for me.</i>

18:45.100 --> 18:50.350
<i>Avoiding danger is not unlike 
cutting oneself off from the world.</i>

18:51.140 --> 18:54.610
<i>That was what this second 
time around has taught me.</i>

18:54.970 --> 18:56.890
I'm not really sure.

18:56.890 --> 19:01.700
But I think this next quest is probably 
the last one for Jasmine and Note.

19:03.220 --> 19:05.780
The guild isn't offering 
much real work now, right?

19:06.250 --> 19:09.700
Normally, I wouldn't mind 
just gathering medicinal herbs,

19:09.700 --> 19:12.700
but if it's the last time, 
we may as well make it memorable.

19:13.970 --> 19:16.110
Your life is the top priority.

19:16.110 --> 19:17.130
Right...

19:17.130 --> 19:22.130
But you're not wrong. Gathering 
medicinal herbs would be a bit dull.

19:22.520 --> 19:23.890
Let's get ready, then.

19:24.420 --> 19:25.810
Thanks, Jasmine!

19:39.550 --> 19:44.160
What did you pay closest attention to 
when getting ready for a quest, Dad?

19:44.160 --> 19:49.580
Good question. Probably being able to 
celebrate and eat together once it was over.

19:49.580 --> 19:50.790
Eating?

19:51.160 --> 19:53.310
The celebrating part is important, too.

19:53.310 --> 19:55.150
Whether the job is a failure or not,

19:55.150 --> 19:57.670
as long as everyone makes it back 
safely, you can still celebrate.

19:59.690 --> 20:01.420
Yeah. You're right.

20:01.800 --> 20:05.220
Come back to me safe,
along with Jasmine.

20:23.780 --> 20:25.410
<i>Sylvie, what are you going to do?</i>

20:25.410 --> 20:28.230
<i>Caves are too clammy! Don't like 'em.</i>

20:28.540 --> 20:29.490
<i>Understood.</i>

20:30.990 --> 20:33.000
<i>Good luck, Arthur.</i>

20:33.270 --> 20:34.350
<i>You too, Sylvie.</i>

20:59.950 --> 21:01.750
It stands to reason

21:01.750 --> 21:04.260
I can't exert perfect control 
over something at this level.

21:04.260 --> 21:06.030
This should suffice, though.

21:06.570 --> 21:09.100
My operations around here are 
reaching their limit, anyway.

21:09.940 --> 21:12.540
Time for one last job.
